Deck: 
Cards 2-10 are "Infantry. They cost their number (Exm 10 is 10 points). They beat cards lower and lose to higher cards.
Aces are a instant kill of any card infront of it (On the first row) no matter the number and is dicared right after.
Face cards are Support. 
Support: You have a row behind your first row where support cards can be placed. They cost no points and have to abilities. they are face down until use.
Jack: allows you to switch cards on your feild before "infantry cards' are revieled.
King: allows you to combine the attack of cards to win one slot but the supporting card will have 0 attack and will lose.
Queen: +2 point for that round to spend on summons.
The support cards have no attack and no defence. They take a hit and are discarded, and when they are used, they are discarded

Rules:
The front: Each team has five slots to place cards. This is then split into two rows. The first row is for numbered card/aces and is effected by aces.
The back row is for support cards only. the far back behind this line is the player's health which numbers 5 hit-points.

Draw: Each player draws three cards to a max of five.
Summon: Each player starts with ten points at the begining of each round. They can then spend those points on summoning numbered cards or can freely summon a support card.
When summoned, the cards are put into a slot face down.
Battle: Cards are flipped upright and the cards in each slot attack the opposing slot. The higher cards win the ingagement and stay on the slot. losing cards are discarded.
if a slot doesn't have a numbered card infront of it; then the attack is absorbed by the support in that slot. If there is not support card in the slot either; then the player loses one hit-point.
Reset: start a new round if no player has reached 0 hit-points.

Reasoning for changes:
We changed the face cards to have unique abilities: Jack: you can swap two cards on the feild (Flipped and non flipped.). Queen: you can discard for an extra 2 points that round. King: you choose a card and a adjacent card to combind attack, but the adjacent card's attack is reduced to 0.
so the face cards are more unique and intresting.
Board expanded to five slots: We found the game getting to grindy and boring so we expaned for more intresting gameplay.
Hand expanded: You still can only draw three cards but can have up to five and start with five. this alows for more actions and one turn stratigy.
